From 7778926b3e0cd5fe76c4f3e1ac39488bce3963b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:37:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: remote notices claim under the link's
 session and fold with local wakes (review t_01a1d013e0411032)

- gateway/kanban_remote_owner: collect(per_link=True) claims each notice under its link's own
  session, the ledger key the Desktop sweep uses; a chat compressed before the card was linked got
  the notice twice (probe: 2 rows in both orders). A notice whose key is already in the lineage is
  acked, never admitted (_drop_written).
- remote notices are Kanban wakes with kanban_cards: they fold with local wakes at the FIFO tail
  both ways; the batch carries every remote key and persists as one kanban_notice row.
- tests: compressed-tip link in both orders, late-group partial adopt/release, 4-event fold (A,R1,B,R2)
  and local-into-remote fold.
